-- title:
--   Descent of a level-M modular function and a residue value
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, let $k$ be a field, let $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $a \in k$ lie in the image of $\mathrm{red}$. Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and let $f$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M`, that is, of the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the image under the coefficient embedding `coeffEmb` of `modularFunctionFieldFull M`, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb{Q})$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the family `divisorExpansions M`. Then there is an intermediate field $K$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that: first, $f$, viewed as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, belongs to `NodeLocalized.fieldOver M K`, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by the constant series with coefficients in $K$ together with the two series $j(q) = q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral power series } \mathtt{jNum})$ and its substitution $q \mapsto q^{M}$; and second, there is an element $x$ of the subring $A \cap K$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\mathrm{red}(x) = a$.
--
--   This is the simultaneous descent step: a modular function of level $M$ with coefficients in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and a prescribed residue value in $k$, are both defined over a single number field $K$, the function lying in $K(j(q), j(q^M))$ and the residue being realised by an element of $A \cap K$. It is used by the node-localisation and place-specialisation results on $X_0(M)$ that need a number-field model in which both the function and the chosen residue value are available.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_finiteDimensional_mem_fieldOver_and_redRestrict_eq_level.lean

